{
 "_comment": [
  "The persisted-format surface that scripts/check_storage_format.py computes, and the record of the approval that admitted it (FMT-1, docs/design-rules.md#fmt-1).",
  "Persisted formats are frozen until Scarab leaves pre-release. This file changes only in a storage format change of its own, approved by the owner in the chat session doing the work in answer to an explicit question asked there before the change was written.",
  "`approval` records that question and the owner's decision, in neutral words and never as a quotation, with their UTC times and the digest of the surface they admit. It is evidence of the approval, never an approval itself. `approval` is null only for the baseline: the surface of main (bc0e4995a, after #994 merged) on 2026-11-14, when the freeze began, which approves nothing."
 ],
 "approval": {
  "question": "Storage format freeze: #1017 (merged) extended the storage-format tests. CodecSuite now pins the V10 snapshot header bytes of the new `11.2` build name (0431312e32), and SnapshotV10MigrationSuite checks that a V10 file recorded under `11.2` is refused by the 11.1 and Leios codecs. No codec, format version, fingerprint or fixture changed. #1008's freeze guard counts those test files as part of the format surface, so main now fails it. May I record this as approved in docs/data/storage-format.json, with this question and your answer and their UTC times, in a `(storage)!` PR of its own?",
  "asked_at": "2026-11-15T18:07:08Z",
  "decision": "Approved: #1017's additions to the storage format tests for the `11.2` build name are admitted under the freeze and recorded here, in a pull request of their own.",
  "decided_at": "2026-11-15T18:09:10Z",
  "surface_sha256": "b0e99302a7272cdd786c2cc1bfd7a59db0b6ea20de449b122df159c572bf0a5c"
 },
